      "visualSettings": "{\"general\":{\"mode\":\"TextPanel\",\"type\":\"text\",\"displayType\":\"default\"},\"series\":{},\"legend\":{\"enabled\":false},\"title\":{\"fontSize\":20},\"text\":{\"format\":\"markdownV2\",\"fontSize\":14,\"backgroundColor\":\"#dfe5e9\",\"textColor\":\"black\",\"verticalAlignment\":\"top\",\"horizontalAlignment\":\"left\",\"showTitle\":false}}",
      "keepVisualSettingsConsistentWithParent": true,
      "panelType": "TextPanel",
      "text": "## Note\n* MetricType\n  * Refer [AWS cost cheatsheet](https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws-cloud-financial-management/understanding-your-aws-cost-datasets-a-cheat-sheet)\n* Estimated\n  * Use **true** to monitor estimated / forecasted cost. \n  * Use **false** to monitor actual cost. Actual cost is available once in a month after invoice is generated.\n* It can take up to 48 hours for [AWS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cost-management/latest/userguide/ce-what-is.html) to generate your billing data. For accuracy Sumo Logic does not present any billing analysis for the last 48-60 hours."
